From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: iio-sensor-proxy 3.9: start polling for early claims (q706f)

Patch for iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 (https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/hadess/iio-sensor-proxy),
applied by scripts/desktop/setup-sensors.sh with 'git apply'. Same licence as
iio-sensor-proxy (GPL-3.0).
---
diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
index 9c7e8cd..9d84e9e 100644
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -779,6 +779,13 @@ name_acquired_handler (GDBusConnection *connection,
 		}
 
 		DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) = sensor_device;
+
+		/* Sensor discovery can iterate the main loop (e.g. the synchronous
+		 * libssc calls), so a client may already have claimed this sensor
+		 * before its driver existed. Start polling for such clients, like
+		 * sensor_changes() does for hotplugged sensors. */
+		if (g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0)
+			driver_set_polling (sensor_device, TRUE);
 	}
 
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
